From: echobot-agent <echobot@rnsbox.local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:43:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] echobot: local LXMF echo bot service (opt-out, on by default)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The box's built-in LXMF presence, like lxmd's init script but simpler: the
daemon (/usr/bin/rnsbox-echobot, shipped by this overlay, like every board
file) attaches to rnsd's shared instance, announces its LXMF destination once
a day by default and echoes every message back — the fastest reachability
check from any LXMF client (NomadNet: Conversations -> the address on the
portal's Echo bot tab). Unlike lxmd/nomadnet it ships enabled: one announce a
day, a small python process, no message store; the min_free_mb floor turns
'tight box' into 'bot off', never 'rnsd OOM-killed'. The daemon polls /proc
for rnsd's shared socket itself, so nothing needs to change in S46wanwatch.
